Subject: [PATCH] runtime: a separate aim pose for each controller (cranvr)

A new control message, CONTROLLER_MOTION_AIM (18), carries the grip and the
aim pose of one hand, each with its velocities. An action space on
/input/aim/pose follows the aim pose, one on /input/grip/pose the grip pose,
for xrLocateSpace and xrLocateViews. A hand that the daemon fed with the
plain CONTROLLER_MOTION has no aim pose, and its aim space follows the grip
pose as before.

A runtime without the patch closes the connection at a message that it does
not know. This runtime therefore writes runtime-features.txt ("aim") next to
the control file when it creates its session, as it writes game-program.txt.
The daemon sends the new message only to a runtime that wrote the file. The
protocol version stays 9.

The test daemon sends the new message for the left hand and a plain one when
the controller comes back. The smoke test locates an aim space and a grip
space of the left hand and checks both.
